# Runtime

Living picture. Update when you add a process, worker, or queue.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  {% if kind == 'service' %}
  {% if frontend == 'vite' %}
  browser[Browser]
  web[Vite / nginx]
  browser --> web
  web -->|"HTTP /api"| http[adapters/http]
  {% else %}
  http[adapters/http]
  {% endif %}
  http --> domain[domain]
  {% if database == 'postgres' %}
  http --> ready[readiness]
  ready --> pg[adapters/postgres]
  pg --> db[(PostgreSQL)]
  {% endif %}
  {% elif kind == 'agent' %}
  cli[CLI]
  cli --> dispatch[run]
  dispatch --> registry[TOOLS registry]
  {% else %}
  pkg["{{ package_name }}"]
  pkg --> hello["hello()"]
  {% endif %}
```

{% if kind == 'service' %}
This is one API process (a modular monolith). Add a capability as `domain/` + `adapters/http/`. Do not add a new Compose service for a new feature unless the human asked.
{% endif %}
{% if kind != 'package' %}
Tools and agents are registered in `src/{{ package_name }}/registry.py`. Do not add a sibling `src/tools/` package.
{% endif %}
{% if frontend == 'vite' %}
The SPA lives in `frontend/`. FastAPI does not render it. Compose (`web`) serves the built assets and proxies `/api` to `api`.
{% endif %}
{% if database == 'postgres' %}
Postgres is a Compose service. Only `adapters/postgres` uses `DATABASE_URL`.
{% endif %}
